  "title": "TreeVQA: A Tree-Structured Execution Framework for Shot Reduction in Variational Quantum Algorithms",
  "abstract": "Variational Quantum Algorithms (VQAs) are promising for near- and intermediate-term quantum computing, but their execution cost is substantial. Each task requires many iterations and numerous circuits per iteration, and real-world applications often involve multiple tasks, scaling with the precision needed to explore the application's energy landscape. This demands an enormous number of execution shots, making practical use prohibitively expensive.",
